import{_ as t,o as a,c as n,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.mm2kvo8B.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Changing targets","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guides/changing-targets.md","filePath":"guides/changing-targets.md","lastUpdated":null}'),s={name:"guides/changing-targets.md"};function o(r,e,d,c,p,h){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="Changing-targets" tabindex="-1">Changing targets <a class="header-anchor" href="#Changing-targets" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Changing targets {#Changing-targets}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Advance a NUTS chain under successive target densities while choosing whether the kernel remains fixed or continues to adapt.</p><h2 id="Fixed-kernel" tabindex="-1">Fixed kernel <a class="header-anchor" href="#Fixed-kernel" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fixed kernel {#Fixed-kernel}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Construct a <code>FixedKernelNUTSState</code> from a warm-up checkpoint or from an RNG and position with a scale operator and step size. <code>fixed_kernel_nuts_step</code> evaluates the supplied target at the saved position before taking the transition. Carry its returned <code>state</code> into the next call. The target may change, but its dimension and coordinate frame must remain compatible with the state.</p><p>A transition is not a posterior fit or a convergence check. A fixed kernel preserves its scale, step size, and tree-depth limit across transitions. When the target remains fixed and draws should be persisted, <code>stream_mcmc</code> provides a disk-backed alternative. Release its mappings with <code>close_stream</code> after copying needed values and before deleting its files.</p><h2 id="Continuous-adaptation" tabindex="-1">Continuous adaptation <a class="header-anchor" href="#Continuous-adaptation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Continuous adaptation {#Continuous-adaptation}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>ContinuousNUTSState</code> and <code>continuous_nuts_step</code> carry decaying position-gradient evidence and update the metric and step size after each transition. Use <code>adapt=false</code> to take a transition with the current kernel held fixed. <code>reposition!</code> changes the saved position; the next transition reevaluates that position under the supplied target.</p><p>A saved position outside the new target&#39;s support is rejected. Leaving support during a leapfrog trajectory is handled as a divergence. Positions collected under different targets do not form one stationary posterior sample, so a pooled mean or ESS of that sequence does not describe a single posterior.</p><p>See the <a href="./../reference/streams">streams and transitions reference</a> for state construction and return fields. The <a href="./../examples/changing-target">changing Gaussian example</a> executes a sequence of fixed-kernel transitions and shows its positions and diagnostics.</p>',9)])])}const u=t(s,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
